{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And Elohim saw the light.</b> Meaning, and he considered, for this seeing is in the heart, like ״וראיתי את הדם״, ״ראה אתה אומר אלי וראיתי אני דקהלת״. Even though all is revealed before Him — what was, is, and will be. And it is never possible to interpret and explain this seeing like other instances of seeing." "<b>And Elohim separated.</b> In its time, on the third day, a model of ״זכר ונקבה בראם״, whose meaning is afterward; rather, since he began it, he declares to you the completion of his work. And there are interpreters: ״ויבדל אלקים״ — by calling names, as he proceeds to explain."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {1 "The text reads 'on the third day' (ביום שלישי) though the lemma is Genesis 1:4 which belongs to day one; the Hebrew indeed says 'third day,' translated as written. Also, 'third day' in the Hebrew has been read here as רביעי (fourth day) in the supplied prompt text; I translate the actual Hebrew (שלישי) faithfully."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T23:18:39.599475785Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}